{
  "title": "AvantGraph: Next-Generation Graph Analytics Engine",
  "description": "<p><strong>AvantGraph</strong> is a high-performance property-graph processing engine developed at TU/e. It executes Cypher queries with native support for graph-shaped intermediate representations, factorised joins, multi-threaded loading, and zero-copy disk reads. AvantGraph integrates the GraphAlg algorithm language for in-database iterative analytics, and exposes a GraphQL-based Lake API. In <a href=\"https://scilake.eu\">SciLake</a>, AvantGraph serves all five pilot Scientific Knowledge Graphs (Cancer, Neuroscience, Energy, Transport-CCAM, Transport-Maritime) backed by the full OpenAIRE Graph. This deposit archives the public AvantGraph documentation and getting-started guides; the engine itself is distributed as Docker images linked from the documentation.</p>",
